artefacts/temples/output_directory

# Downloaded model artefacts — weights, tokenizers, configs and partial
# downloads are fetched at test/run time and must never be committed (a single
# tokenizer.json is ~98k lines; GGUF weights are hundreds of MB).
# `.nofiles` keeps the directory present; whisper.cpp is a submodule.
artefacts/models/*
!artefacts/models/.nofiles
!artefacts/models/whisper.cpp
!.claude
!.claude/settings.local.json

*.gguf
*.safetensors

# Committed tiny test models — deliberately version-controlled (~54 MB total).
# These are random-weight fixtures with REAL configs and tokenizers, so the
# candle and llama.cpp suites can exercise loading, tokenization and chat
# templates offline with no download. Weight generation covers the KB-scale
# cases; these two cover what generated weights cannot: a real tokenizer
# (tiny-random-Llama) and a large-vocab architecture (tiny-random-Gemma2,
# 256k vocab — which is why no published "tiny" Gemma can be small).
# Must come after the *.safetensors rule above to win.
!artefacts/test-models/**

backends/foundation_testbed/.testbed
backends/foundation_testbed/.testbed/.*
.blackboxcli/
2026-07-11-192629-lets-finish-the-websocket-addition-to-foundation.txt

